WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.510
In a Catholic parish, Mass is
celebrated every day of the week.

2
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.070
Down the road, a Baptist church may
hold the Lord's Supper once a month.

3
00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.430
Both look back to one
night, and one command:

4
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.890
Do this in memory of me.

5
00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.770
So why do some churches
share bread every day,

6
00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.090
and others only once a month?

7
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:23.520
In this mission, you'll read
Luke's account of the Last Supper,

8
00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:26.110
the only Gospel with two cups.

9
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.180
Then you'll step inside a Catholic
Mass and a Baptist Lord's Supper,

10
00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:32.400
and see what each church does.

11
00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:38.110
Your mission: explain why Christians who
obey one command celebrate it so differently.
